Third-party material
====================

Vial-GPU / vial-gui — https://github.com/vial-kb/vial-gui
    SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
    Copyright (C) the Vial contributors

    The VIA/Vial protocol implementation under `svalboard/protocol/`, the KLE
    deserialiser in `svalboard/protocol/kle.py`, the keycode tables under
    `svalboard/protocol/keycodes/`, and the QMK settings schema in
    `svalboard/protocol/qmk_settings.py` are adapted from vial-gui. Adapted
    files carry their original SPDX headers. vial-gui is GPL-2.0-or-later, and
    this work exercises the "or later" option to combine it with PyQt6 under
    GPL-3.0.

vial-qmk / Svalboard firmware — https://github.com/svalboard/vial-qmk
    SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
    Copyright (C) the QMK, Vial and Svalboard contributors

    Protocol constants, the Svalboard `0xEE` command channel, the Vial unlock
    sequence, matrix geometry and firmware capacity limits were read from this
    source and are reproduced here as interface facts.

QMK Firmware — https://github.com/qmk/qmk_firmware
    SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later

    Keycode names, values and descriptions derive from QMK's headers.


A note on KeyBard
=================

KeyBard (https://github.com/captdeaf/keybard and
https://github.com/svalboard/keybard-ng) is the web configurator this program
replaces. Neither repository carries a LICENSE file, so no code from either is
used here. KeyBard was consulted only as a description of observable behaviour
and wire formats — facts about how the hardware speaks, not expression.
